<!--Post: 2663--><!--Time: 1103892350-->
<!--p:--><tr bgcolor="#f7f7f7"><td valign=top width=200><a name="POST2663"><font face="Verdana" size="1"><b><!--email--><!--/email--><!--name-->Vdubguy<!--/name--></b></a><br>Username: <!--field:uname-->Vdubguy<!--/field--><br><br>Registered: <!--field:registered-->12-2004<!--/field--><br><!--field:ip_address--><!--/field--></font></font></td><td valign=top><font face="Verdana" size="1"><table width=100% border=0 cellspacing=0 cellpadding=0><tr><td align=left><font face="Verdana" size="1">Posted on Friday, December 24, 2004 - 4:45 am: &nbsp;&nbsp;</font></td><td align=right></td></tr></table><hr noshade size=0><!--Text-->An idea about his noncommunication all those years. Do you think is possible that in 86 he may have seen/read about/had knowledge of, any new technology that may have implicated him. Besides DNA i dont know of anything else that may have been developed around that time that might have scared him into seclusion. Any thoughts? <!--/Text--></td></tr>
<!--/Post: 2663-->
<!--Post: 2672--><!--Time: 1103905641-->
<!--p:--><tr bgcolor="#cccccc"><td valign=top width=200><a name="POST2672"><font face="Verdana" size="1"><b><!--email--><!--/email--><!--name-->Scbenson2001<!--/name--></b></a><br>Username: <!--field:uname-->Scbenson2001<!--/field--><br><br>Registered: <!--field:registered-->6-2004<!--/field--><br><!--field:ip_address--><!--/field--></font></font></td><td valign=top><font face="Verdana" size="1"><table width=100% border=0 cellspacing=0 cellpadding=0><tr><td align=left><font face="Verdana" size="1">Posted on Friday, December 24, 2004 - 8:27 am: &nbsp;&nbsp;</font></td><td align=right></td></tr></table><hr noshade size=0><!--Text-->video recorders came out in &#39;86 <BR>maybe he videotaped the murder.<!--/Text--></td></tr>
<!--/Post: 2672-->
<!--Post: 2677--><!--Time: 1103913780-->
<!--p:--><tr bgcolor="#f7f7f7"><td valign=top width=200><a name="POST2677"><font face="Verdana" size="1"><b><!--email--><!--/email--><!--name-->Ryddik<!--/name--></b></a><br>Username: <!--field:uname-->Ryddik<!--/field--><br><br>Registered: <!--field:registered-->12-2004<!--/field--><br><!--field:ip_address--><!--/field--></font></font></td><td valign=top><font face="Verdana" size="1"><table width=100% border=0 cellspacing=0 cellpadding=0><tr><td align=left><font face="Verdana" size="1">Posted on Friday, December 24, 2004 - 10:43 am: &nbsp;&nbsp;</font></td><td align=right></td></tr></table><hr noshade size=0><!--Text-->video recorders were big and bulky when they first came out I think it would be kinda hard to lug a 10 pound video recorder to and from a murder and not be seen<!--/Text--></td></tr>
<!--/Post: 2677-->
<!--Post: 2686--><!--Time: 1103923890-->
<!--p:--><tr bgcolor="#cccccc"><td valign=top width=200><a name="POST2686"><font face="Verdana" size="1"><b><!--email--><!--/email--><!--name-->Vdubguy<!--/name--></b></a><br>Username: <!--field:uname-->Vdubguy<!--/field--><br><br>Registered: <!--field:registered-->12-2004<!--/field--><br><!--field:ip_address--><!--/field--></font></font></td><td valign=top><font face="Verdana" size="1"><table width=100% border=0 cellspacing=0 cellpadding=0><tr><td align=left><font face="Verdana" size="1">Posted on Friday, December 24, 2004 - 1:31 pm: &nbsp;&nbsp;</font></td><td align=right></td></tr></table><hr noshade size=0><!--Text-->my wonder was &#39;what was new at that time that might be used to identify him.&#39; If somehting technological &#39;scared&#39; him into seclusion possibly...<!--/Text--></td></tr>
<!--/Post: 2686-->
<!--Post: 2725--><!--Time: 1104027822-->
<!--p:--><tr bgcolor="#f7f7f7"><td valign=top width=200><a name="POST2725"><font face="Verdana" size="1"><b><!--email--><!--/email--><!--name-->Secret_squirrel<!--/name--></b></a><br>Username: <!--field:uname-->Secret_squirrel<!--/field--><br><br>Registered: <!--field:registered-->12-2004<!--/field--><br><!--field:ip_address--><!--/field--></font></font></td><td valign=top><font face="Verdana" size="1"><table width=100% border=0 cellspacing=0 cellpadding=0><tr><td align=left><font face="Verdana" size="1">Posted on Saturday, December 25, 2004 - 6:23 pm: &nbsp;&nbsp;</font></td><td align=right></td></tr></table><hr noshade size=0><!--Text-->Some of the tech introduced and becoming available at the time was, generally speaking, the cellular system &#40;1983&#41;, 911 emergency number &#40;1968&#41;, and possible the NCIC or National Crime Information Center. <BR> <BR>The cellular system was introduced in 1983, and although not yet nationwide, it was becoming available in bigger cities such as Wichita.  Knowing that the &#34;land phone lines&#34; were cut insured no outside communications from the victims.  The advent of cellular service may have been enough for him to through in the towel. <BR> <BR>Secondly, a single emergency number was being implemented nationwide.  These familiar digits that we know as 911 were becoming the more and more common throughout the country.  Beginning in 1968, many large cities were getting on this sytem.  I havent been able to find when it was actually implemented by the City of Wichita, but quite possibly not until around the mid 1980&#39;s.  However, what is known as Enhanced 911 was not introduced until approximately mid to late 80&#39;s.  Most smaller communties didnt have this sytem due to the complexity but today we have a version of it right in our own homes.  In a nutshell, Enhanced 911 is caller ID however with a bit of a twist.  If a person dials 911 to report an emergency their number and location is immediately identified. Furthermore, it also would tip off a dipatcher to send police for any caller who has been disconnected, become unconcious, cannot speak or has hung up.  Police would immediately be sent to the location of the caller.  Basically what Im trying to say is that if a person was able to make it to the phone before he cut the lines and at very least dial the three digits, a police unit would be dispatched to investigate. <BR> <BR>Finally, and Im not sure about this, but the NCIC became available sometime around the early 80&#39;s I believe.  This is the FBI&#39;s National Crime Information Center which is a nationwide database containing all sorts of incriminating information.  The database contains anything from criminal history to missing persons etc.  However, one must be in the record from some prior activity/history to be of any value to authorities.  Although, I know of a case where a serial rapist was caught using NCIC and was not in the database it seems unlikely this would scare anyone into remission. <BR> <BR>These are just what I came up with off the top of my head and I hope everyone will through out some other ideas.  Merry Christmas!!! <BR> <BR>By the way, Im working all night so please post so I have something to read and think about. <BR>Thanks!!!  <!--/Text--></td></tr>
<!--/Post: 2725-->
<!--Post: 2737--><!--Time: 1104038625-->
<!--p:--><tr bgcolor="#cccccc"><td valign=top width=200><a name="POST2737"><font face="Verdana" size="1"><b><!--email--><!--/email--><!--name-->Vdubguy<!--/name--></b></a><br>Username: <!--field:uname-->Vdubguy<!--/field--><br><br>Registered: <!--field:registered-->12-2004<!--/field--><br><!--field:ip_address--><!--/field--></font></font></td><td valign=top><font face="Verdana" size="1"><table width=100% border=0 cellspacing=0 cellpadding=0><tr><td align=left><font face="Verdana" size="1">Posted on Saturday, December 25, 2004 - 9:23 pm: &nbsp;&nbsp;</font></td><td align=right></td></tr></table><hr noshade size=0><!--Text-->Very interesting...I jsut wonder if the 911 system may have had something to do with him disappearing. Cellular was introduced in Chicago in about 84ish. By 86 some of the larger citys were getting the systems. With air-time being as costly as it originally was Im sure that these women werent the types to have cell service.  <!--/Text--></td></tr>
<!--/Post: 2737-->
<!--Post: 2805--><!--Time: 1104159876-->
<!--p:--><tr bgcolor="#f7f7f7"><td valign=top width=200><a name="POST2805"><font face="Verdana" size="1"><b><!--email--><!--/email--><!--name-->Secret_squirrel<!--/name--></b></a><br>Username: <!--field:uname-->Secret_squirrel<!--/field--><br><br>Registered: <!--field:registered-->12-2004<!--/field--><br><!--field:ip_address--><!--/field--></font></font></td><td valign=top><font face="Verdana" size="1"><table width=100% border=0 cellspacing=0 cellpadding=0><tr><td align=left><font face="Verdana" size="1">Posted on Monday, December 27, 2004 - 7:04 am: &nbsp;&nbsp;</font></td><td align=right></td></tr></table><hr noshade size=0><!--Text-->I definitely agree in saying that they probably didnt have cell service.  Cellular service wasnt practical until the 90&#39;s.  I can remember the big bag phones carried by executives which seemed to be more of a novelty or a status symbol.  Anyway, is it possble that due to any of their occupations, some of the victims may have have been on call and would have cellular service from time to time through their company?  Just a thought!!   <BR> <BR>Also, Internet service became available in the early 90&#39;s.  Although rudimentary, did provide free and uncensored topics right in your own home.  This is back before the pay sites were catching on and anyone could view just about anything if they had a connection. <BR> <BR>As far as the Enhanced 911 sytem is concerned, one would have to have prior knowledge of the mechanics of it.  The average citizen whom are not in the business only know that 911 is the number that everyone calls for emergencies.  Even today most people dont how the system works, which is why we still, from time to time receive emergencies calls from civilians who call the fire stations directly rather than 911.<!--/Text--></td></tr>
<!--/Post: 2805-->
<!--Post: 2828--><!--Time: 1104174808-->
<!--p:--><tr bgcolor="#cccccc"><td valign=top width=200><a name="POST2828"><font face="Verdana" size="1"><b><!--email--><!--/email--><!--name-->Vdubguy<!--/name--></b></a><br>Username: <!--field:uname-->Vdubguy<!--/field--><br><br>Registered: <!--field:registered-->12-2004<!--/field--><br><!--field:ip_address--><!--/field--></font></font></td><td valign=top><font face="Verdana" size="1"><table width=100% border=0 cellspacing=0 cellpadding=0><tr><td align=left><font face="Verdana" size="1">Posted on Monday, December 27, 2004 - 11:13 am: &nbsp;&nbsp;</font></td><td align=right></td></tr></table><hr noshade size=0><!--Text-->They more than likely had pagers, if anything. Eliminating the potential of cell phones. Internet wasnt even close to public use at that point. <!--/Text--></td></tr>
<!--/Post: 2828-->
<!--Post: 2830--><!--Time: 1104174906-->
<!--p:--><tr bgcolor="#f7f7f7"><td valign=top width=200><a name="POST2830"><font face="Verdana" size="1"><b><!--email--><!--/email--><!--name-->Vdubguy<!--/name--></b></a><br>Username: <!--field:uname-->Vdubguy<!--/field--><br><br>Registered: <!--field:registered-->12-2004<!--/field--><br><!--field:ip_address--><!--/field--></font></font></td><td valign=top><font face="Verdana" size="1"><table width=100% border=0 cellspacing=0 cellpadding=0><tr><td align=left><font face="Verdana" size="1">Posted on Monday, December 27, 2004 - 11:15 am: &nbsp;&nbsp;</font></td><td align=right></td></tr></table><hr noshade size=0><!--Text-->Which leads me back to my original point...Did BTK think that a potential technology could reveal him? OR did he just disappear? Im not sure...too many possible scenarios...<!--/Text--></td></tr>
<!--/Post: 2830-->
<!--Post: 2844--><!--Time: 1104183031-->
<!--p:--><tr bgcolor="#cccccc"><td valign=top width=200><a name="POST2844"><font face="Verdana" size="1"><b><!--email--><!--/email--><!--name-->Secret_squirrel<!--/name--></b></a><br>Username: <!--field:uname-->Secret_squirrel<!--/field--><br><br>Registered: <!--field:registered-->12-2004<!--/field--><br><!--field:ip_address--><!--/field--></font></font></td><td valign=top><font face="Verdana" size="1"><table width=100% border=0 cellspacing=0 cellpadding=0><tr><td align=left><font face="Verdana" size="1">Posted on Monday, December 27, 2004 - 1:30 pm: &nbsp;&nbsp;</font></td><td align=right></td></tr></table><hr noshade size=0><!--Text-->I thought this was rather interesting given the years that it occured.  DNA was beginning to be used in a variety of ways in 1985 and soon found its way into the forensic field.  I have attached a link below of one of the first cases where DNA evidence was used. You can probably bet that DNA being used as an exoneration and conviction device made nationwide news.  You can also bet that BTK is somewhat of a DNA guru and has studied it extensively. He probably wishes that he had&#39;nt gotten so excited at those crime scenes.  Who&#39;dev ever thunk!! See the link below and click on chapter 2. <BR> <BR><a href="http://www.crimelibrary.com/forensics/dna/" target=_top>http://www.crimelibrary.com/forensics/dna/</a> <BR> <BR><!--/Text--></td></tr>
<!--/Post: 2844-->
<!--Post: 3007--><!--Time: 1104369440-->
<!--p:--><tr bgcolor="#f7f7f7"><td valign=top width=200><a name="POST3007"><font face="Verdana" size="1"><b><!--email--><!--/email--><!--name-->Bulldog87<!--/name--></b></a><br>Username: <!--field:uname-->Bulldog87<!--/field--><br><br>Registered: <!--field:registered-->12-2004<!--/field--><br><!--field:ip_address--><!--/field--></font></font></td><td valign=top><font face="Verdana" size="1"><table width=100% border=0 cellspacing=0 cellpadding=0><tr><td align=left><font face="Verdana" size="1">Posted on Wednesday, December 29, 2004 - 5:17 pm: &nbsp;&nbsp;</font></td><td align=right></td></tr></table><hr noshade size=0><!--Text-->How many samples of btk&#39;s DNA do police have? the idea of DNA was around long before 86. Could the DNA at the crime scenes be fabricated? Simply left to throw the police and investgators off?<!--/Text--></td></tr>
<!--/Post: 3007-->
<!--Post: 3018--><!--Time: 1104373160-->
<!--p:--><tr bgcolor="#cccccc"><td valign=top width=200><a name="POST3018"><font face="Verdana" size="1"><b><!--email--><!--/email--><!--name-->Secret_squirrel<!--/name--></b></a><br>Username: <!--field:uname-->Secret_squirrel<!--/field--><br><br>Registered: <!--field:registered-->12-2004<!--/field--><br><!--field:ip_address--><!--/field--></font></font></td><td valign=top><font face="Verdana" size="1"><table width=100% border=0 cellspacing=0 cellpadding=0><tr><td align=left><font face="Verdana" size="1">Posted on Wednesday, December 29, 2004 - 6:19 pm: &nbsp;&nbsp;</font></td><td align=right></td></tr></table><hr noshade size=0><!--Text-->Im not exactly sure how many actual samples that WPD are holding as evidence.  Im assuming from what I have read that there was DNA present at every scene.   <BR> <BR>DNA has been around for probably about 100 years but it was&#39;nt completly understood.  It wasnt until 1987 when it was actually used as criminal evidence as a genetic fingerprint.  I wouldnt think that anyone prior to the 1980&#39;s who wasnt into forensics or medicine would have ever heard of DNA or gave it much thought.  However, someone with a criminal invetigations background may have knowledge of its uses.  I never thought of it until now, but I guess the scenes could have been fabricated for all the right reasons for the killer.  It makes sense if someone did their homework.  Then again, prior to 1987ish, I wonder if anyone knew including experts that it was possible to trace and prosecute someone using DNA technology since it had never been tested? <BR> <BR>Given the profile of BTK and assuming that it is accurate I would say that the DNA left at the scenes belongs to him.  Our knowledge of the crimes leads us to believe that he was sexually motivated, or maybe thats what he wants us to think.<!--/Text--></td></tr>
<!--/Post: 3018-->
<!--Post: 3044--><!--Time: 1104380346-->
<!--p:--><tr bgcolor="#f7f7f7"><td valign=top width=200><a name="POST3044"><font face="Verdana" size="1"><b><!--email--><!--/email--><!--name-->Bulldog87<!--/name--></b></a><br>Username: <!--field:uname-->Bulldog87<!--/field--><br><br>Registered: <!--field:registered-->12-2004<!--/field--><br><!--field:ip_address--><!--/field--></font></font></td><td valign=top><font face="Verdana" size="1"><table width=100% border=0 cellspacing=0 cellpadding=0><tr><td align=left><font face="Verdana" size="1">Posted on Wednesday, December 29, 2004 - 8:19 pm: &nbsp;&nbsp;</font></td><td align=right></td></tr></table><hr noshade size=0><!--Text-->Yea i agree thats its a reach. My thought was that if btk had been an MP, Forensic or medical background he might realize this as an effective way to throw off the investigation. Not neccessarily DNA, but blood type ect. &#40;he just lucked out on dna&#41; He could comfortably take the test and be eliminated as a suspect.  This could be the reason why btk is so cocky and the investigators seem to struggle. I thought they got the DNA off of one specific crime scene, but I have no idea. I agree to his perverse motivation, but he is also extremely calculating and clever.<!--/Text--></td></tr>
<!--/Post: 3044-->
<!--Post: 3046--><!--Time: 1104380741-->
<!--p:--><tr bgcolor="#cccccc"><td valign=top width=200><a name="POST3046"><font face="Verdana" size="1"><b><!--email--><!--/email--><!--name-->Secret_squirrel<!--/name--></b></a><br>Username: <!--field:uname-->Secret_squirrel<!--/field--><br><br>Registered: <!--field:registered-->12-2004<!--/field--><br><!--field:ip_address--><!--/field--></font></font></td><td valign=top><font face="Verdana" size="1"><table width=100% border=0 cellspacing=0 cellpadding=0><tr><td align=left><font face="Verdana" size="1">Posted on Wednesday, December 29, 2004 - 8:25 pm: &nbsp;&nbsp;</font></td><td align=right></td></tr></table><hr noshade size=0><!--Text-->&#34;but he is also extremely calculating and clever.&#34; <BR> <BR>It certainly seems so at this point Bulldog. Anything is possible in this game so I think that you have a good theory.<!--/Text--></td></tr>
<!--/Post: 3046-->
<!--Post: 3079--><!--Time: 1104432738-->
<!--p:--><tr bgcolor="#f7f7f7"><td valign=top width=200><a name="POST3079"><font face="Verdana" size="1"><b><!--email--><!--/email--><!--name-->Ryddik<!--/name--></b></a><br>Username: <!--field:uname-->Ryddik<!--/field--><br><br>Registered: <!--field:registered-->12-2004<!--/field--><br><!--field:ip_address--><!--/field--></font></font></td><td valign=top><font face="Verdana" size="1"><table width=100% border=0 cellspacing=0 cellpadding=0><tr><td align=left><font face="Verdana" size="1">Posted on Thursday, December 30, 2004 - 10:52 am: &nbsp;&nbsp;</font></td><td align=right></td></tr></table><hr noshade size=0><!--Text-->Has anyone really put into perspective when handguns &#40;personnel and gang usage&#41; began showing up more in the Wichita area. In my city there was a huge increase in violent crime such as shootings and consealed weapons in the mid to late 80&#39;s and early 90&#39;s. BTK may have thought it too risky to break into homes any more if the chance of him getting shot was on the back of his mind.<!--/Text--></td></tr>
